  "id": "bailes_religiosos_la_tirana",
  "name": "Bailes religiosos de La Tirana (Norte Grande devotional dance bands)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Devotional dance music of the Fiesta de La Tirana in the Tarapacá pampa, held each July for the Virgen del Carmen and attended by hundreds of dance societies (bailes religiosos) from Iquique and the towns of the Chilean north. Each baile has its own band: brass bands of trumpets, trombones and tubas with bass drum, snare and cymbals (the sousaphone card stands in for the bass horn) play for the diabladas, morenos, who swing wooden ratchets, and other costumed dances, while lakitas play large panpipes over bass drums, and the dancers sing hymns of greeting and farewell to the Virgin.",
  "recipe": "classic modern bailes religiosos de la tirana, carnival Processional, andean branch. horn section ensemble trumpet, trombone, sousaphone, bombo andino, snare drum, andean tradition paired rows interlocking siku panpipes. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
